WEBVTT

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:01.555
Meet Fizzlayer.

00:00:01.555 --> 00:00:04.612
The intelligence layer for your physical world.

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.496
Connect a sensor.

00:00:07.496 --> 00:00:08.480
Ask a question.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.564
Get a call when something needs your attention.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:16.355
Start with the devices you already have.

00:00:16.355 --> 00:00:24.520
Fizzlayer brings phones, ESP32s, Raspberry Pis, and any HTTPS
source into one clear workspace.

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:30.004
See live readings at a glance, from cold storage to air
quality.

00:00:30.004 --> 00:00:35.562
Sample streams are clearly labeled, so you can explore before
your hardware arrives.

00:00:36.812 --> 00:00:38.014
Then just ask Fizz.

00:00:38.014 --> 00:00:44.972
Answers are grounded in your actual sensor data, giving you
useful context without digging through dashboards.

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:48.580
Set a threshold in seconds.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:56.700
When Cold Room rises above eight degrees, Fizzlayer calls the
right person, so a small change does not become a big problem.

00:01:01.012 --> 00:01:03.494
Sending data is straightforward.

00:01:03.494 --> 00:01:09.388
Each device gets its own revocable key and posts readings over
secure HTTPS.

00:01:11.212 --> 00:01:13.645
Connect your own agents through MCP.

00:01:13.645 --> 00:01:19.660
They can work with live sensor context, while device keys and
phone numbers stay private.

00:01:21.212 --> 00:01:27.999
From one sensor to an entire operation, Fizzlayer turns real-
world signals into useful action.

00:01:27.999 --> 00:01:29.876
Your world has a sidekick.
